# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Doors and windows cut by a section (drawing quality plan, item 15): a
# cut detail in NEN-ISO 128 style instead of a bare gap. A 300 mm wall 6 m
# long, standing free (so an outer wall, its exterior side to the south),
# with a 1.2 by 1.5 m window (sill 0.9, frame 0.05), a 0.9 by 2.1 m door
# (frame 0.05) and a 0.6 by 2.1 m window down to the floor, each crossed
# square by a section running north from 2 m south of the wall (so the
# wall's line is 2 m along it, the outdoors before it).
#
# At 1:50, the window: the frame's head (2400 to 2450) and bottom rail (900
# to 950) as cut rectangles 114 mm deep on the wall's line, the glass on the
# frame's middle between them, an outer sill sloping from the frame out
# 30 mm past the outer face with its nose 30 mm below the sill, and a window
# board 30 mm thick out 30 mm past the inner face. The door: its head (2100
# to 2150), a threshold 20 mm high, and the leaf 40 mm thick shut flush with
# the frame's inner face (it opens inward), from the threshold to the head.
# The floor-length window: no sills. A section through a jamb cuts the jamb
# over the whole height; a slanting one widens the cut by 1 / sin(angle);
# one missing the openings draws none. At 1:100 the frame is one outline
# over the opening's height with the glass or leaf as one line, no sills or
# threshold; at 1:200 a window is its glass line, a door nothing. A window
# on an upper storey in a wall with a base offset stands at the storey's
# elevation plus its sill, as the void and its projected frame. A window
# system hosted in a window is cut where the line crosses its parts, as
# the plan draws them, the window's sills kept: its profiles 10 mm inside
# the rough opening, on the ground floor and on the upper storey; a door
# system in a door is not cut over the door. With walls built on both
# sides the wall is inner: no sills, no threshold. Recorded on paper the cuts are
# black in the cut pen (0.50 mm) and the glass and leaf black in the thin
# pen (0.18 mm), in the section panel's drawing and in the section's
# viewport on a sheet (at 1:100, the outline); grey when the window
# category is halftone; nothing when it is hidden or the wall is hidden
# (HH).
import ui/shell/bim_app_parts.dl

function check opening cuts {boolean:passed} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function opening cuts {a 64 bit floating-point number:value} is near {a 64 bit floating-point number:wanted}:
    execute:
        return (the absolute value of (value - wanted)) < 0.0001

function opening cuts spot {cad vector2:spotValue} is at {a 64 bit floating-point number:wantedX} {a 64 bit floating-point number:wantedY}:
    execute:
        return (opening cuts (spotValue's x) is near wantedX) and (opening cuts (spotValue's y) is near wantedY)

# Whether `pairs` holds the segment between the two points, either way round.
function opening cuts {a pointer to a list:pairs} hold from {a 64 bit floating-point number:ax} {a 64 bit floating-point number:ay} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:bx} {a 64 bit floating-point number:by}:
    execute:
        set holdFound to false
        set pairCursor to 0
        loop while (pairCursor + 1) < (the length of pairs):
            set startSpot to the item at pairCursor in pairs
            set endSpot to the item at (pairCursor + 1) in pairs
            set matchesForward to (opening cuts spot startSpot is at ax ay) and (opening cuts spot endSpot is at bx by)
            set matchesBackward to (opening cuts spot startSpot is at bx by) and (opening cuts spot endSpot is at ax ay)
            if matchesForward or matchesBackward:
                set holdFound to true
            set pairCursor to pairCursor + 2
        return holdFound

# Whether a rectangle from (`lowX`, `lowY`) to (`highX`, `highY`) has all
# four sides in `pairs`.
function opening cuts {a pointer to a list:pairs} hold box {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowX} {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowY} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:highX} {a 64 bit floating-point number:highY}:
    execute:
        set bottomSide to opening cuts pairs hold from lowX lowY to highX lowY
        set rightSide to opening cuts pairs hold from highX lowY to highX highY
        set topSide to opening cuts pairs hold from highX highY to lowX highY
        set leftSide to opening cuts pairs hold from lowX highY to lowX lowY
        return (bottomSide and rightSide) and (topSide and leftSide)

# How many stroked segments on `canvas` run between the two points (either
# way round, to a hundredth of a unit) in a batch `breadth` wide coloured
# (`red`, `green`, `blue`). A stroke is six corners: its start is the middle
# of the first two, its end the middle of the third and sixth.
function the opening cuts strokes on {bim canvas record:canvas} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:ax} {a 64 bit floating-point number:ay} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:bx} {a 64 bit floating-point number:by} wide {a 64 bit floating-point number:breadth} coloured {integer:red}, {integer:green} and {integer:blue}:
    execute:
        set found to 0
        loop batchCursor from 0 to the length of (canvas's batches's values):
            set recorded to the item at batchCursor in (canvas's batches's values)
            set sameColour to ((recorded's red = red) and (recorded's green = green)) and (recorded's blue = blue)
            if (recorded's stroked and sameColour) and ((the absolute value of (recorded's breadth - breadth)) < 0.0001):
                set corners to recorded's pixels's values
                set cornerCursor to 0
                loop while (cornerCursor + 5) < (the length of corners):
                    set cornerA to the item at cornerCursor in corners
                    set cornerB to the item at (cornerCursor + 1) in corners
                    set cornerC to the item at (cornerCursor + 2) in corners
                    set cornerF to the item at (cornerCursor + 5) in corners
                    set firstX to (cornerA's x + cornerB's x) * 0.5
                    set firstY to (cornerA's y + cornerB's y) * 0.5
                    set secondX to (cornerC's x + cornerF's x) * 0.5
                    set secondY to (cornerC's y + cornerF's y) * 0.5
                    set matchesForward to (((the absolute value of (firstX - ax)) < 0.01) and ((the absolute value of (firstY - ay)) < 0.01)) and (((the absolute value of (secondX - bx)) < 0.01) and ((the absolute value of (secondY - by)) < 0.01))
                    set matchesBackward to (((the absolute value of (firstX - bx)) < 0.01) and ((the absolute value of (firstY - by)) < 0.01)) and (((the absolute value of (secondX - ax)) < 0.01) and ((the absolute value of (secondY - ay)) < 0.01))
                    if matchesForward or matchesBackward:
                        set found to found + 1
                    set cornerCursor to cornerCursor + 6
        return found

# The segment from section point (`ax`, `ay`) to (`bx`, `by`) drawn through
# `transform` on `canvas` in a batch `breadth` wide, coloured (`red`,
# `green`, `blue`); black.
function opening cuts {bim canvas record:canvas} strokes {a 64 bit floating-point number:ax} {a 64 bit floating-point number:ay} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:bx} {a 64 bit floating-point number:by} through {bim drawing transform record:transform} wide {a 64 bit floating-point number:breadth} coloured {integer:red}, {integer:green} and {integer:blue}:
    execute:
        set firstPixel to the bim pixel of (a cad vector2 with x ax and y ay) through transform
        set secondPixel to the bim pixel of (a cad vector2 with x bx and y by) through transform
        return (the opening cuts strokes on canvas from firstPixel's x firstPixel's y to secondPixel's x secondPixel's y wide breadth coloured red, green and blue) > 0

function opening cuts {bim canvas record:canvas} strokes {a 64 bit floating-point number:ax} {a 64 bit floating-point number:ay} to {a 64 bit floating-point number:bx} {a 64 bit floating-point number:by} through {bim drawing transform record:transform} wide {a 64 bit floating-point number:breadth}:
    execute:
        return opening cuts canvas strokes ax ay to bx by through transform wide breadth coloured 0, 0 and 0

# Whether any segment in `pairs` reaches below height `lowest`.
function opening cuts {a pointer to a list:pairs} reach below {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowest}:
    execute:
        set reachFound to false
        loop spotCursor from 0 to the length of pairs:
            if (the item at spotCursor in pairs)'s y < (lowest - 0.0001):
                set reachFound to true
        return reachFound

# How many stroke corners `canvas` holds, in all its stroked batches.
function the opening cuts corners on {bim canvas record:canvas}:
    execute:
        set cornerTotal to 0
        loop batchCursor from 0 to the length of (canvas's batches's values):
            set recorded to the item at batchCursor in (canvas's batches's values)
            if recorded's stroked:
                set cornerTotal to cornerTotal + (the length of (recorded's pixels's values))
        return cornerTotal

# View `viewId` drawn at 1:`scaleWanted`, its display kept.
function rescale opening cuts view {a 64 bit integer:viewId} to {integer:scaleWanted} in {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        set viewFound to the bim view index of viewId in (@intrinsic("dereference", target))
        set displayKept to (the item at viewFound's position in (target's views's values))'s displayMode
        ignore set bim view viewId scale to scaleWanted and display to displayKept in target

function show opening cut {bim opening section record:openingCut} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        print ((((the string form of "  ") + label) + (the string form of ": cut segments ")) + ((the string form of ((the length of (openingCut's cuts's values)) / 2)) + ((the string form of ", glass ") + ((the string form of ((the length of (openingCut's glazing's values)) / 2)) + ((the string form of ", leaf ") + (the string form of ((the length of (openingCut's leaves's values)) / 2))))))) as a line

set editor to a new bim editor
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set ground to editor's levelId
set layerValues to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "brick", 0.3)) to layerValues
set brickType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Brick 300") with layerValues to target
free layerValues
set frontWall to add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 0.0) to target
set windowType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window 1200") sized 1.2 by 1.5 with sill 0.9 and frame 0.05 to target
set windowId to add bim opening typed windowType in frontWall at 1.5 to target
set doorType to add bim door type named (the string form of "Door 900") sized 0.9 by 2.1 with frame 0.05 to target
set doorId to add bim opening typed doorType in frontWall at 4.5 to target
set tallType to add bim opening type named (the string form of "Window 600 to the floor") sized 0.6 by 2.1 with sill 0.0 and frame 0.05 to target
set tallId to add bim opening typed tallType in frontWall at 5.4 to target
set windowValue to the item at (the bim opening index of windowId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's openings's values)
set doorValue to the item at (the bim opening index of doorId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's openings's values)
set tallValue to the item at (the bim opening index of tallId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's openings's values)

# The window, crossed square at its middle: the wall's line is 2 m along
# the section, its exterior (south) side before it, so a metre toward the
# exterior is a metre back along the line; the frame runs from 1.943 to
# 2.057.
set modelNow to editor's documentValue's current
set windowCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
show opening cut windowCut named (the string form of "window")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (windowCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.45) named (the string form of "window head cut 2400 to 2450 across the frame's depth")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (windowCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 0.9 to 2.057 0.95) named (the string form of "window bottom rail cut 900 to 950")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (windowCut's glazing's values) hold from 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4) named (the string form of "glass on the frame's middle between rail and head")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts (windowCut's cuts's values) hold from 1.943 0.93 to 1.82 0.9) and (opening cuts (windowCut's cuts's values) hold from 1.82 0.87 to 1.85 0.87)) named (the string form of "outer sill slopes out 30 mm past the outer face, its nose below the sill")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (windowCut's cuts's values) hold box 2.057 0.9 to 2.18 0.93) named (the string form of "window board inside, 30 mm past the inner face")
check opening cuts ((the length of (windowCut's leaves's values)) = 0) named (the string form of "a window has no leaf")

# A window system hosted in the window: its frame and glass left out, the
# sills kept.
set unframedCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) framed false at drawing scale 50.0
show opening cut unframedCut named (the string form of "window unframed")
check opening cuts (((the length of (unframedCut's glazing's values)) = 0) and (opening cuts (unframedCut's cuts's values) hold box 2.057 0.9 to 2.18 0.93)) named (the string form of "unframed: no frame or glass, the sills kept")

# The door: head, threshold, and the leaf shut on the inner side.
set doorCut to the bim section cut of opening doorValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
show opening cut doorCut named (the string form of "door")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (doorCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 2.1 to 2.057 2.15) named (the string form of "door head cut 2100 to 2150")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (doorCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 0.0 to 2.057 0.02) named (the string form of "threshold 20 mm high on an outer wall")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (doorCut's leaves's values) hold box 2.017 0.02 to 2.057 2.1) named (the string form of "leaf 40 mm thick, flush with the frame's inner face")
check opening cuts ((the length of (doorCut's glazing's values)) = 0) named (the string form of "a door has no glass")
set bim setting (bim door swing setting) of doorId to (1 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target
set outwardCut to the bim section cut of opening doorValue in (editor's documentValue's current) from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
check opening cuts (opening cuts (outwardCut's leaves's values) hold box 1.943 0.02 to 1.983 2.1) named (the string form of "opening outward, the leaf lies on the outer side")
set bim setting (bim door swing setting) of doorId to (0 as a 64 bit integer) keeping true in target

# Through the window's jamb (20 mm into it): the jamb over the whole height.
set jambCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 0.87 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 0.87 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
show opening cut jambCut named (the string form of "jamb")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts (jambCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 0.9 to 2.057 2.45) and ((the length of (jambCut's glazing's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "a jamb is cut over the whole height")

# Slanting at 45 degrees through the window's middle: everything across the
# wall is the square root of 2 wider.
set slantCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 0.5 and y -1.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.5 and y 1.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
set rootTwo to the square root of 2.0
check opening cuts (opening cuts (slantCut's cuts's values) hold box (rootTwo - (0.057 * rootTwo)) 2.4 to (rootTwo + (0.057 * rootTwo)) 2.45) named (the string form of "a slanting section widens the frame's cut")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (slantCut's glazing's values) hold from rootTwo 0.95 to rootTwo 2.4) named (the string form of "and keeps the glass on the wall's line")

# Between the openings, and past the line's end: nothing.
set missCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 3.0 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 3.0 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
set shortCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -1.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
check opening cuts (((the length of (missCut's cuts's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (shortCut's cuts's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "a section missing the opening draws none of it")

# A window down to the floor on the outer wall: head and bottom rail, no
# sills (an outer sill's nose would hang below the floor).
set tallCut to the bim section cut of opening tallValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 5.4 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 5.4 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
show opening cut tallCut named (the string form of "window to the floor")
check opening cuts ((((the length of (tallCut's cuts's values)) = 16) and (opening cuts (tallCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 0.0 to 2.057 0.05)) and ((opening cuts (tallCut's cuts's values) reach below 0.0) = false)) named (the string form of "a window to the floor: frame only, nothing below the floor")

# At 1:100 the frame is one outline over the opening's height, the glass
# or the leaf (on the leaf's middle, 2.037) one line, no sills or
# threshold.
set outlineWindow to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 100.0
set outlineDoor to the bim section cut of opening doorValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 100.0
show opening cut outlineWindow named (the string form of "window at 1:100")
show opening cut outlineDoor named (the string form of "door at 1:100")
check opening cuts (((the length of (outlineWindow's cuts's values)) = 8) and (opening cuts (outlineWindow's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 0.9 to 2.057 2.45)) named (the string form of "1:100: the window's frame one outline, no profiles or sills")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (outlineWindow's glazing's values) hold from 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4) named (the string form of "1:100: the glass one line in it")
check opening cuts (((the length of (outlineDoor's cuts's values)) = 8) and (opening cuts (outlineDoor's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 0.0 to 2.057 2.15)) named (the string form of "1:100: the door's frame one outline, no threshold")
check opening cuts (((the length of (outlineDoor's leaves's values)) = 2) and (opening cuts (outlineDoor's leaves's values) hold from 2.037 0.0 to 2.037 2.1)) named (the string form of "1:100: the leaf one line on its middle")

# At 1:200 a window is its glass line over the opening's height; a door
# its gap.
set coarseWindow to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 200.0
set coarseDoor to the bim section cut of opening doorValue in modelNow from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 200.0
check opening cuts ((((the length of (coarseWindow's cuts's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (coarseWindow's glazing's values)) = 2)) and (opening cuts (coarseWindow's glazing's values) hold from 2.0 0.9 to 2.0 2.45)) named (the string form of "1:200: a window is one line")
check opening cuts ((((the length of (coarseDoor's cuts's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (coarseDoor's leaves's values)) = 0)) and ((the length of (coarseDoor's glazing's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "1:200: a door is its gap")

# On an upper storey (3 m) in a wall standing 0.25 m above it: the window
# stands at the storey plus its sill (3900 to 5450), where the evaluation
# cuts its void, not at the wall's base plus its sill.
set upperLevel to add bim level named (the string form of "First floor") at 3.0 with height 3.0 to target
set upperWall to add bim wall typed brickType on upperLevel from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 10.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 10.0) to target
set upperWindowId to add bim opening typed windowType in upperWall at 1.5 to target
set upperFound to the bim wall index of upperWall in (editor's documentValue's current)
set raisedWall to the item at upperFound's position in (target's walls's values)
set raisedWall's baseOffset to 0.25
replace item at index upperFound's position in (target's walls's values) with raisedWall
set upperWindow to the item at (the bim opening index of upperWindowId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's openings's values)
set upperCut to the bim section cut of opening upperWindow in (editor's documentValue's current) from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 8.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 12.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
check opening cuts ((opening cuts (upperCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 5.4 to 2.057 5.45) and (opening cuts (upperCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.943 3.9 to 2.057 3.95)) named (the string form of "upper storey, raised wall: head 5400-5450, rail 3900-3950")
set upperShown to editor
set upperShown's hasSection to true
set upperShown's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 8.0
set upperShown's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 12.0
set upperVoid to the bim section box of opening upperWindow for upperShown
check opening cuts ((upperVoid's valid and (opening cuts (upperVoid's low's y) is near 3.9)) and (opening cuts (upperVoid's high's y) is near 5.45)) named (the string form of "and the void stands at the same heights")
# The projected frame beyond the cut (`the bim opening view of`) stands
# there too, not 0.25 m higher on the wall's base.
set upperView to the bim opening view of upperWindow in (editor's documentValue's current)
set viewLowest to 1e300
set viewHighest to -1e300
loop viewCursor from 0 to the length of (upperView's frame's positions's values):
    set viewCorner to the item at viewCursor in (upperView's frame's positions's values)
    set viewLowest to the minimum of viewLowest and (viewCorner's z)
    set viewHighest to the maximum of viewHighest and (viewCorner's z)
print ((the string form of "  projected frame from ") + ((the string form of viewLowest) + ((the string form of " to ") + (the string form of viewHighest)))) as a line
check opening cuts ((upperView's valid and (opening cuts viewLowest is near 3.9)) and (opening cuts viewHighest is near 5.45)) named (the string form of "and the projected frame stands at the same heights")

# Recorded as the section panel records it, on paper at 1:50 (a unit to
# the millimetre): black cut pen 0.50 mm, black thin pen 0.18 mm.
set windowSection to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) to target
set doorSection to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0) to target
rescale opening cuts view windowSection to 50 in target
rescale opening cuts view doorSection to 50 in target
refresh bim editor (the address of editor)
set paperTransform to @intrinsic("construct", a bim drawing transform record, (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0), (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0), 1000.0 / 50.0)
set shown to editor
set shown's hasSection to true
set shown's sectionViewId to windowSection
set shown's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0
set shown's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0
set shown's sectionRules to the bim rules of view (the item at (the bim view index of windowSection in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)) in editor's documentValue's current
set windowCanvas to a new bim canvas
set windowCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of shown through paperTransform on (the address of windowCanvas)
print ((the string form of "  window canvas batches ") + (the string form of (the length of (windowCanvas's batches's values)))) as a line
check opening cuts (opening cuts windowCanvas strokes 1.943 0.9 to 2.057 0.9 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the bottom rail's underside at the sill, cut pen")
check opening cuts (opening cuts windowCanvas strokes 1.943 0.95 to 2.057 0.95 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the bottom rail's top, cut pen")
check opening cuts (opening cuts windowCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the head's underside, cut pen")
check opening cuts (opening cuts windowCanvas strokes 1.943 2.45 to 2.057 2.45 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the head's top at the rough opening's head, cut pen")
check opening cuts (opening cuts windowCanvas strokes 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.18) named (the string form of "paper: the glass in the thin pen")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts windowCanvas strokes 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5) = false) named (the string form of "paper: the glass not in the cut pen")

set shown's sectionViewId to doorSection
set shown's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0
set shown's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0
set doorCanvas to a new bim canvas
set doorCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of shown through paperTransform on (the address of doorCanvas)
check opening cuts ((opening cuts doorCanvas strokes 1.943 2.1 to 2.057 2.1 through paperTransform wide 0.5) and (opening cuts doorCanvas strokes 1.943 0.02 to 2.057 0.02 through paperTransform wide 0.5)) named (the string form of "paper: door head and threshold, cut pen")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts doorCanvas strokes 2.017 0.02 to 2.017 2.1 through paperTransform wide 0.18) and (opening cuts doorCanvas strokes 2.057 0.02 to 2.057 2.1 through paperTransform wide 0.18)) named (the string form of "paper: the leaf's faces in the thin pen")

# On screen, the model review: the cuts black, the glass blue.
set shown's sectionViewId to windowSection
set shown's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0
set shown's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0
set screenCanvas to a new bim canvas
draw bim openings in section of shown through paperTransform on (the address of screenCanvas)
loop batchCursor from 0 to the length of (screenCanvas's batches's values):
    set recorded to the item at batchCursor in (screenCanvas's batches's values)
    print ((the string form of "  screen batch ") + ((the string form of recorded's red) + ((the string form of " ") + ((the string form of recorded's green) + ((the string form of " ") + ((the string form of recorded's blue) + ((the string form of " wide ") + (the string form of recorded's breadth)))))))) as a line

# On a sheet at its own scale, 1:100: the section's viewport records the
# frame's outline in the cut pen and the glass in the thin pen, and no
# profile edges.
rescale opening cuts view windowSection to 100 in target
set sheetId to add bim sheet numbered (the string form of "A-301") named (the string form of "Sections") on paper 2 landscape true to target
ignore place bim view windowSection on sheet sheetId at (a cad vector2 with x 200.0 and y 200.0) looking at (the bim model centre of view windowSection in editor's documentValue's current) in target
set sheetValue to the item at (the bim sheet index of sheetId in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (target's sheets's values)
set placedView to the item at 0 in (sheetValue's viewports's values)
set sheetCorner to a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 420.0
set sheetTransform to @intrinsic("construct", a bim drawing transform record, (the bim sheet pixel of placedView's centre from sheetCorner at 1.0), placedView's modelCentre, 1000.0 / (the bim scale of view windowSection in editor's documentValue's current))
print ((the string form of "  sheet scale 1:") + (the string form of ((the bim scale of view windowSection in editor's documentValue's current) as an integer))) as a line
set emptyAtlas to @intrinsic("construct", a bim text atlas record, @intrinsic("construct", a graphics texture, 0 as a pointer to a byte, 0, 0), an empty list of a bim text face record, 0, 0, an empty list of a bim icon cell record, an empty bim message catalogue, an empty list of a pointer, -1)
set scene to an empty list of a bim scene mesh record
set sheetCanvas to a new bim canvas
record bim sheet viewport 0 of sheetValue of editor among scene from sheetCorner at 1.0 using emptyAtlas on (the address of sheetCanvas)
check opening cuts ((opening cuts sheetCanvas strokes 1.943 0.9 to 1.943 2.45 through sheetTransform wide 0.5) and (opening cuts sheetCanvas strokes 1.943 2.45 to 2.057 2.45 through sheetTransform wide 0.5)) named (the string form of "sheet at 1:100: the frame's outline in the cut pen")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts sheetCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through sheetTransform wide 0.5) = false) named (the string form of "sheet at 1:100: no head profile")
check opening cuts (opening cuts sheetCanvas strokes 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4 through sheetTransform wide 0.18) named (the string form of "sheet: the glass in the thin pen")

# A window system hosted in a third window 3.05 m along the wall (rough
# opening x 2.4 to 3.7, 900 to 2450): recipe 34, a double casement of
# timber profiles 90 wide and 139 deep, with a 10 mm joint round it, so
# its outer faces stand 10 mm inside the rough opening (910 to 2440). The
# section through its left casement (x 2.75) cuts the system's own parts,
# as the plan draws them, in place of the window's frame and glass; the
# window's sills stay. The expected numbers come from the recipe and the
# rough opening, not from the system's parts.
set systemWindowId to add bim opening typed windowType in frontWall at 3.05 to target
set systemId to ensure bim window system in opening systemWindowId typed 34 with joint (10 as a 64 bit integer) in target
check opening cuts (systemId != the bim refused id) named (the string form of "window system: recipe 34 hosted in the window")
set systemModel to editor's documentValue's current
set systemValue to the item at (the bim curtain index of systemId in systemModel)'s position in (systemModel's curtains's values)
set systemCut to the bim section cut of system systemValue in systemModel from (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y 2.0) at drawing scale 50.0 resolving 20.0
show opening cut systemCut named (the string form of "window system")
set systemLowest to 1e300
set systemHighest to -1e300
set systemNearest to 1e300
set systemFarthest to -1e300
loop systemCursor from 0 to the length of (systemCut's cuts's values):
    set systemSpot to the item at systemCursor in (systemCut's cuts's values)
    set systemLowest to the minimum of systemLowest and (systemSpot's y)
    set systemHighest to the maximum of systemHighest and (systemSpot's y)
    set systemNearest to the minimum of systemNearest and (systemSpot's x)
    set systemFarthest to the maximum of systemFarthest and (systemSpot's x)
print ((the string form of "  system profiles from ") + ((the string form of systemLowest) + ((the string form of " to ") + ((the string form of systemHighest) + ((the string form of ", across ") + ((the string form of systemNearest) + ((the string form of " to ") + (the string form of systemFarthest)))))))) as a line
loop systemCursor from 0 to ((the length of (systemCut's cuts's values)) / 8):
    set boxLow to the item at (systemCursor * 8) in (systemCut's cuts's values)
    set boxHigh to the item at ((systemCursor * 8) + 4) in (systemCut's cuts's values)
    print ((the string form of "  profile ") + ((the string form of boxLow's x) + ((the string form of " ") + ((the string form of boxLow's y) + ((the string form of " to ") + ((the string form of boxHigh's x) + ((the string form of " ") + (the string form of boxHigh's y)))))))) as a line
check opening cuts ((opening cuts systemLowest is near 0.91) and (opening cuts systemHighest is near 2.44)) named (the string form of "window system: its profiles reach from 910 to 2440, 10 mm inside the rough opening")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts systemNearest is near 1.9305) and (opening cuts systemFarthest is near 2.0695)) named (the string form of "window system: its profiles 139 mm deep across the wall's line")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (systemCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.9305 2.35 to 2.0695 2.44) named (the string form of "window system: its head frame 90 mm high, 2350 to 2440")
check opening cuts (opening cuts (systemCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.9305 0.91 to 2.0695 1.0) named (the string form of "window system: its sill frame 90 mm high, 910 to 1000")
check opening cuts (((the length of (systemCut's glazing's values)) >= 2) and (opening cuts ((the item at 0 in (systemCut's glazing's values))'s x) is near 2.0)) named (the string form of "window system: its glass one line on the wall's line")
set systemOutline to the bim section cut of system systemValue in systemModel from (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y 2.0) at drawing scale 100.0 resolving 10.0
check opening cuts (((the length of (systemOutline's cuts's values)) = 8) and (opening cuts (systemOutline's cuts's values) hold box 1.9305 0.91 to 2.0695 2.44)) named (the string form of "window system at 1:100: one outline round its profiles, 910 to 2440")
set systemCoarse to the bim section cut of system systemValue in systemModel from (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y 2.0) at drawing scale 200.0 resolving 5.0
check opening cuts (((the length of (systemCoarse's cuts's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (systemCoarse's glazing's values)) >= 2)) named (the string form of "window system at 1:200: its glass lines only")
set systemMiss to the bim section cut of system systemValue in systemModel from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) at drawing scale 50.0 resolving 20.0
check opening cuts (((the length of (systemMiss's cuts's values)) = 0) and ((the length of (systemMiss's glazing's values)) = 0)) named (the string form of "window system: a section beside it cuts none of it")
# At 1:20 on paper (50 units to the metre) the glazing beads and seals do
# not resolve, as in the plan: the same profiles as at 1:50, no 3 mm boxes.
set systemFine to the bim section cut of system systemValue in systemModel from (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y 2.0) at drawing scale 20.0 resolving 50.0
check opening cuts ((the length of (systemFine's cuts's values)) = (the length of (systemCut's cuts's values))) named (the string form of "window system at 1:20 on paper: no glazing beads or seals that do not resolve")
# Drawn as the section panel draws it, on paper at 1:50: the system's head
# frame's top at 2440 in the cut pen, the window board kept, the glass in
# the thin pen, and none of the window's own frame (its head at 2400).
set systemSection to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y 2.0) to target
rescale opening cuts view systemSection to 50 in target
refresh bim editor (the address of editor)
set systemShown to editor
set systemShown's hasSection to true
set systemShown's sectionViewId to systemSection
set systemShown's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y -2.0
set systemShown's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 2.75 and y 2.0
set systemShown's sectionRules to the bim rules of view (the item at (the bim view index of systemSection in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)) in editor's documentValue's current
set systemCanvas to a new bim canvas
set systemCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of systemShown through paperTransform on (the address of systemCanvas)
check opening cuts (opening cuts systemCanvas strokes 1.9305 2.44 to 2.0695 2.44 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the system's head frame's top at 2440 in the cut pen")
check opening cuts (opening cuts systemCanvas strokes 1.9305 0.91 to 2.0695 0.91 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the system's sill frame's underside at 910 in the cut pen")
check opening cuts (opening cuts systemCanvas strokes 2.18 0.9 to 2.18 0.93 through paperTransform wide 0.5) named (the string form of "paper: the window board kept")
check opening cuts (opening cuts systemCanvas strokes 2.0 ((the item at 0 in (systemCut's glazing's values))'s y) to 2.0 ((the item at 1 in (systemCut's glazing's values))'s y) through paperTransform wide 0.18) named (the string form of "paper: the system's glass in the thin pen")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts systemCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5) = false) named (the string form of "paper: no frame of the window's own")

# The same system in the upper storey's window (storey at 3 m, wall raised
# 0.25 m, void 3900 to 5450, left casement at x 1.2): its profiles stand on
# the storey, 3910 to 5440, with the window's sills, not 3 m lower.
set upperSystemId to ensure bim window system in opening upperWindowId typed 34 with joint (10 as a 64 bit integer) in target
check opening cuts (upperSystemId != the bim refused id) named (the string form of "upper window system: recipe 34 hosted")
set upperModel to editor's documentValue's current
set upperSystem to the item at (the bim curtain index of upperSystemId in upperModel)'s position in (upperModel's curtains's values)
set upperSystemCut to the bim section cut of system upperSystem in upperModel from (a cad vector2 with x 1.2 and y 8.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.2 and y 12.0) at drawing scale 50.0 resolving 20.0
set upperLowest to 1e300
set upperHighest to -1e300
loop systemCursor from 0 to the length of (upperSystemCut's cuts's values):
    set upperLowest to the minimum of upperLowest and ((the item at systemCursor in (upperSystemCut's cuts's values))'s y)
    set upperHighest to the maximum of upperHighest and ((the item at systemCursor in (upperSystemCut's cuts's values))'s y)
print ((the string form of "  upper system profiles from ") + ((the string form of upperLowest) + ((the string form of " to ") + (the string form of upperHighest)))) as a line
check opening cuts (((opening cuts upperLowest is near 3.91) and (opening cuts upperHighest is near 5.44)) and (opening cuts (upperSystemCut's cuts's values) hold box 1.9305 5.35 to 2.0695 5.44)) named (the string form of "upper window system: profiles 3910 to 5440 on the storey, its head frame 5350 to 5440")
set upperSection to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x 1.2 and y 8.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.2 and y 12.0) to target
rescale opening cuts view upperSection to 50 in target
refresh bim editor (the address of editor)
set upperDrawn to editor
set upperDrawn's hasSection to true
set upperDrawn's sectionViewId to upperSection
set upperDrawn's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 1.2 and y 8.0
set upperDrawn's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 1.2 and y 12.0
set upperDrawn's sectionRules to the bim rules of view (the item at (the bim view index of upperSection in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)) in editor's documentValue's current
set upperCanvas to a new bim canvas
set upperCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of upperDrawn through paperTransform on (the address of upperCanvas)
check opening cuts ((opening cuts upperCanvas strokes 1.9305 5.44 to 2.0695 5.44 through paperTransform wide 0.5) and (opening cuts upperCanvas strokes 2.18 3.9 to 2.18 3.93 through paperTransform wide 0.5)) named (the string form of "paper, upper storey: the system's head at 5440 and the window board at 3900")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts upperCanvas strokes 1.9305 2.44 to 2.0695 2.44 through paperTransform wide 0.5) = false) named (the string form of "paper, upper storey: nothing of the system 3 m below")

# A door system (recipe 28, as the window-system action hosts in a door)
# in a door on the upper wall at 4.0: the door keeps its own frame,
# threshold and leaf and the system is not cut over them, as the plan
# keeps the door's symbol; the drawing is the same with it as without.
set upperDoorId to add bim opening typed doorType in upperWall at 4.0 to target
set upperDoorSection to add bim section view from (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 8.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 12.0) to target
rescale opening cuts view upperDoorSection to 50 in target
refresh bim editor (the address of editor)
set doorDrawn to editor
set doorDrawn's hasSection to true
set doorDrawn's sectionViewId to upperDoorSection
set doorDrawn's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 8.0
set doorDrawn's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 4.0 and y 12.0
set doorDrawn's sectionRules to the bim rules of view (the item at (the bim view index of upperDoorSection in editor's documentValue's current)'s position in (editor's documentValue's current's views's values)) in editor's documentValue's current
set bareDoorCanvas to a new bim canvas
set bareDoorCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of doorDrawn through paperTransform on (the address of bareDoorCanvas)
set doorSystemId to ensure bim window system in opening upperDoorId typed 28 with joint (10 as a 64 bit integer) in target
check opening cuts (doorSystemId != the bim refused id) named (the string form of "door system: recipe 28 hosted in the door")
set doorDrawn's documentValue to editor's documentValue
set hostedDoorCanvas to a new bim canvas
set hostedDoorCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of doorDrawn through paperTransform on (the address of hostedDoorCanvas)
set bareCorners to the opening cuts corners on bareDoorCanvas
set hostedCorners to the opening cuts corners on hostedDoorCanvas
print ((the string form of "  door stroke corners ") + ((the string form of bareCorners) + ((the string form of " bare, ") + ((the string form of hostedCorners) + (the string form of " with a system"))))) as a line
check opening cuts ((bareCorners > 0) and (hostedCorners = bareCorners)) named (the string form of "door system: the door's section drawn as without it, nothing cut over it")
check opening cuts ((opening cuts hostedDoorCanvas strokes 1.943 5.1 to 2.057 5.1 through paperTransform wide 0.5) and (opening cuts hostedDoorCanvas strokes 2.017 3.02 to 2.017 5.1 through paperTransform wide 0.18)) named (the string form of "door system: the door's head and leaf kept")

# Walls on both sides make the front wall an inner wall: no sills, no
# threshold.
ignore add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y -3.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y -3.0) to target
ignore add bim wall typed brickType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 3.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 6.0 and y 3.0) to target
set innerModel to editor's documentValue's current
set innerWindowCut to the bim section cut of opening windowValue in innerModel from (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
set innerDoorCut to the bim section cut of opening doorValue in innerModel from (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y -2.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 4.5 and y 2.0) framed true at drawing scale 50.0
show opening cut innerWindowCut named (the string form of "inner window")
show opening cut innerDoorCut named (the string form of "inner door")
check opening cuts (((the length of (innerWindowCut's cuts's values)) = 16) and ((opening cuts (innerWindowCut's cuts's values) hold box 2.057 0.9 to 2.18 0.93) = false)) named (the string form of "an inner wall's window: frame only, no sills")
check opening cuts (((the length of (innerDoorCut's cuts's values)) = 8) and (opening cuts (innerDoorCut's leaves's values) hold box 2.017 0.0 to 2.057 2.1)) named (the string form of "an inner wall's door: no threshold, the leaf from the floor")

# The draw's visibility, on paper at 1:50: halftone greys the cut, a hidden
# window category or the wall hidden (HH) leaves the window out.
set shown's sectionViewId to windowSection
set shown's sectionFirst to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y -2.0
set shown's sectionSecond to a cad vector2 with x 1.5 and y 2.0
rescale opening cuts view windowSection to 50 in target
set shown's documentValue to editor's documentValue
toggle bim category (bim window category) halftone in (the address of (shown's sectionRules))
set faintCanvas to a new bim canvas
set faintCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of shown through paperTransform on (the address of faintCanvas)
check opening cuts ((opening cuts faintCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5 coloured 150, 150 and 150) and ((opening cuts faintCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5) = false)) named (the string form of "halftone: the head's profile grey, not black")
check opening cuts (opening cuts faintCanvas strokes 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.18 coloured 150, 150 and 150) named (the string form of "halftone: the glass grey")
toggle bim category (bim window category) halftone in (the address of (shown's sectionRules))
toggle bim category (bim window category) visibility in (the address of (shown's sectionRules))
set hiddenCanvas to a new bim canvas
set hiddenCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of shown through paperTransform on (the address of hiddenCanvas)
check opening cuts (((opening cuts hiddenCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5) = false) and ((opening cuts hiddenCanvas strokes 2.0 0.95 to 2.0 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.18) = false)) named (the string form of "windows hidden: no cut drawn")
toggle bim category (bim window category) visibility in (the address of (shown's sectionRules))
set hiddenWall to an empty list of a 64 bit integer
append frontWall to hiddenWall
ignore hide bim elements hiddenWall in view windowSection among (shown's hiddenElements's values)
free hiddenWall
set wallHiddenCanvas to a new bim canvas
set wallHiddenCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim openings in section of shown through paperTransform on (the address of wallHiddenCanvas)
check opening cuts ((opening cuts wallHiddenCanvas strokes 1.943 2.4 to 2.057 2.4 through paperTransform wide 0.5) = false) named (the string form of "the wall hidden (HH): no cut drawn")
